<instruction name="HADDPS">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Packed Single Precision Floating-Point Horizontal Add</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261278">
   <string>Adds the single precision floating-point values in the first and second dwords of the destination operand and stores the result in the first dword of the destination operand.</string></para>
  <para unique="1261279">
   <string>Adds single precision floating-point values in the third and fourth dword of the destination operand and stores the result in the second dword of the destination operand.</string></para>
  <para unique="1261280">
   <string>Adds single precision floating-point values in the first and second dword of the source operand and stores the result in the third dword of the destination operand.</string></para>
  <para unique="1261281">
   <string>Adds single precision floating-point values in the third and fourth dword of the source operand and stores the result in the fourth dword of the destination operand. </string></para>
  <para unique="1261282">
   <string>In 64-bit mode, use of the REX.R prefix permits this instruction to access additional registers (XMM8-XMM15).</string></para>
  <para unique="1261286">
   <string>See </string><link linkend="60346: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-11. HADDPS: Packed Single-FP Horizontal Add"><string>Figure&#160;3&#8209;14</string></link><string> for HADDPS; see </string><link linkend="20026: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-22. VHADDPS operation"><string>Figure&#160;3&#8209;15</string></link><string> for VHADDPS.</string></para>
  <table>
